# Caddy config for orchestrator.ai-storystudio.com — TLS termination and
# reverse proxy in front of the orchestrator container.
#
# CANONICAL COPY. The live file is /opt/qm-orchestrator/caddy/Caddyfile; the
# two must be kept identical — see docs/qm-orchestrator-vps-access.md §3.
#
# The ACME contact address is read from the environment rather than written
# here: this repository is public, and a contact email in git history is
# scrapeable and effectively permanent. It is set as ACME_EMAIL in
# /opt/qm-orchestrator/.env (chmod 600, not in git) and forwarded to the caddy
# service by orchestrator/deploy/docker-compose.yml. `{$VAR}` is Caddy's own
# environment placeholder, substituted when the config is parsed.
#
# The fallback is load-bearing, not decoration: `email` with no argument is a
# PARSE ERROR, so a bare `{$ACME_EMAIL}` would take TLS down on the next
# restart if the .env line were ever missing — a terrible failure mode for the
# public entrypoint. With a default the config always parses; the real contact
# still comes from .env. Caught by `caddy validate` on 2026-09-19 before it
# ever reached a running proxy.
{
    email {$ACME_EMAIL:noreply@ai-storystudio.com}
}
orchestrator.ai-storystudio.com {
    reverse_proxy orchestrator:8080
    encode zstd gzip
    header {
        Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
        X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
        -Server
    }
}
